{"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"anchor":"Modules"},{"title":"Testing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"],"anchor":"Testing"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"code":"SourceLocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"code":"records","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"code":"batch(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"code":"Consent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"code":"ConsentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"code":"Constraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"code":"RejectionReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"rejectionReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"code":"trackLifecycle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"code":"Sampler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"code":"SamplingDropReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"code":"SampleRateKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"code":"Enricher.application()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"device()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"operatingSystem()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"locale()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" imports every module but ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},{"text":", a product of its own for apps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that already use GRDB; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"},{"text":", whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" macro derives an event’s conformances","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},{"text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"collection","title":"Traffluent","externalID":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","title":"Identifying People","abstract":[{"text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","title":"Changing an Event","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","abstract":[{"text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"TrackingPlans","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","title":"CollectorEncoding","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://UIKitTracking/document